1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,040
Imagine tomorrow's class needs a short practice paper.

2
00:00:03,605 --> 00:00:04,880
You have a topic in mind,

3
00:00:05,325 --> 00:00:08,140
but the questions, marking scheme, student responses

4
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:10,620
and feedback are all in different places.

5
00:00:11,105 --> 00:00:14,060
This is a tour of how FocusED connects that work.

6
00:00:14,605 --> 00:00:17,120
We'll start with creating and checking an assessment,

7
00:00:17,325 --> 00:00:18,975
take it into an online classroom,

8
00:00:19,465 --> 00:00:21,215
and then follow the student's side:

9
00:00:21,625 --> 00:00:22,300
lessons,

10
00:00:22,425 --> 00:00:23,100
practice,

11
00:00:23,445 --> 00:00:24,880
exam rooms and study tools.

12
00:00:25,445 --> 00:00:28,440
We'll also look at university planning, course editing

13
00:00:28,765 --> 00:00:31,420
and the different account permissions. Some screens in

14
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:34,400
this tour use clearly labelled demonstration data.

15
00:00:34,905 --> 00:00:36,840
They show the actual interface without

16
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:38,820
exposing a real student's work.

17
00:00:39,325 --> 00:00:41,280
Public lessons and exam rooms

18
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,160
are recorded from the live platform.

19
00:00:43,745 --> 00:00:45,440
Let's start in the exam creator.

20
00:00:46,105 --> 00:00:48,455
First decide what you want the paper to assess.

21
00:00:49,005 --> 00:00:50,660
A chapter on algebra is a more

22
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:53,700
useful starting point than a request for a difficult test.

23
00:00:54,305 --> 00:00:56,005
Choose the relevant qualification,

24
00:00:56,365 --> 00:01:00,080
subject and scope, then set the structure and maximum marks.

25
00:01:00,705 --> 00:01:02,255
You can build a paper manually.

26
00:01:02,745 --> 00:01:04,640
Write the question, add any parts,

27
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,420
assign the marks and enter

28
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:08,820
the expected answer or marking criteria.

29
00:01:09,585 --> 00:01:11,400
A short numerical question and

30
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:14,460
an explanation question need different marking instructions.

31
00:01:15,285 --> 00:01:17,560
Keep those instructions clear enough that someone

32
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:20,220
else could apply them. AI assistance can

33
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:22,505
produce a draft where your account permits it.

34
00:01:22,925 --> 00:01:24,480
That draft still belongs on

35
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:27,040
your review desk. Read each question.

36
00:01:27,405 --> 00:01:28,605
Work through the answer.

37
00:01:28,985 --> 00:01:31,580
Check that the wording matches the syllabus and

38
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:34,380
that the marks reflect what a student must actually do.

39
00:01:34,885 --> 00:01:36,420
The paper remains editable.

40
00:01:36,845 --> 00:01:37,745
Change a question,

41
00:01:38,065 --> 00:01:39,060
repair an answer,

42
00:01:39,625 --> 00:01:41,180
adjust the marks or replace an

43
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:42,840
item that doesn't fit the lesson.

44
00:01:43,485 --> 00:01:45,540
The point is to prepare the assessment you

45
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:48,620
need, rather than accept the first generated version.

46
00:01:49,185 --> 00:01:51,220
When it is ready, use the student version for

47
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:54,180
the task and keep the answers or marking scheme separate.

48
00:01:54,685 --> 00:01:57,835
Printing and export support the same paper outside the browser.

49
00:01:58,205 --> 00:01:59,820
Before sharing it, check the final

50
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:01,240
layout and the total marks.

51
00:02:01,785 --> 00:02:03,420
Now look at the exam checker.

52
00:02:03,745 --> 00:02:04,595
It needs context:

53
00:02:05,105 --> 00:02:06,380
what was asked, how it should

54
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:08,365
be marked and what the student answered.

55
00:02:08,805 --> 00:02:10,580
A response on its own cannot tell

56
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:13,660
a checker which method marks the teacher intended to award.

57
00:02:14,185 --> 00:02:16,185
Bring in the paper and marking criteria,

58
00:02:16,765 --> 00:02:19,265
then the student's work using the supported input.

59
00:02:19,685 --> 00:02:22,440
Typed responses are useful for a quick demonstration;

60
00:02:23,305 --> 00:02:26,060
document or image inputs need legible text

61
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:28,540
and a careful check of anything extracted.

62
00:02:29,305 --> 00:02:32,620
The useful part of the result is the question-level explanation.

63
00:02:33,485 --> 00:02:35,740
Look at what the response actually contains,

64
00:02:36,265 --> 00:02:39,460
which criteria it meets and why a mark was withheld.

65
00:02:40,185 --> 00:02:41,960
If a student used the right method

66
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:44,600
but made an arithmetic slip, the marking scheme

67
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,000
should determine how that affects the result.

68
00:02:47,545 --> 00:02:50,645
Review the feedback before treating it as a teaching decision.

69
00:02:51,185 --> 00:02:53,940
Exact objective answers can be checked directly.

70
00:02:54,825 --> 00:02:57,820
Subjective AI marking is provisional, and a

71
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:00,520
teacher should verify it against the work and rubric.

72
00:03:00,985 --> 00:03:04,440
A confident-looking number is not a substitute for that review.

73
00:03:04,985 --> 00:03:06,335
The next step is practical:

74
00:03:06,685 --> 00:03:08,380
decide what the learner should do again.

75
00:03:08,685 --> 00:03:10,140
A short correction task can be

76
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:12,275
more useful than repeating the whole paper.

77
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:15,015
Keep the explanation tied to the specific error

78
00:03:15,015 --> 00:03:16,955
so the student knows what to change.

79
00:03:17,465 --> 00:03:19,400
Move that assessment into the classroom.

80
00:03:19,765 --> 00:03:22,180
A teacher creates or manages a class, and

81
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:24,080
students use the class code to join.

82
00:03:24,605 --> 00:03:26,640
Membership and teaching controls keep

83
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:29,220
the class's work separate from unrelated accounts.

84
00:03:29,765 --> 00:03:32,940
Within the class, organise members and prepare an assignment.

85
00:03:33,545 --> 00:03:36,245
Choose the assessment and make the instructions clear:

86
00:03:36,725 --> 00:03:38,100
what should students complete,

87
00:03:38,285 --> 00:03:39,360
what should they submit

88
00:03:39,465 --> 00:03:40,415
and when is it due?

89
00:03:40,805 --> 00:03:44,160
A class name alone doesn't explain the task. Online

90
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:47,360
sessions can have a time and an external meeting link.

91
00:03:47,945 --> 00:03:51,040
The meeting button opens the service chosen by the teacher.

92
00:03:51,725 --> 00:03:55,140
FocusED organises the session and its learning tasks;

93
00:03:55,685 --> 00:03:58,035
the video call happens in that meeting service.

94
00:03:58,465 --> 00:04:00,640
During a lesson, open the lesson board.

95
00:04:01,185 --> 00:04:03,135
Put the learning goal, the current task

96
00:04:03,205 --> 00:04:05,500
and a timer on a screen the class can follow.

97
00:04:05,805 --> 00:04:07,980
For example, students might have six

98
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:10,440
minutes to attempt one question, then compare

99
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:13,380
their reasoning. The board presents that structure.

100
00:04:14,065 --> 00:04:17,140
It does not silently collect answers or record attendance.

101
00:04:17,805 --> 00:04:19,420
When work and results are ready,

102
00:04:19,765 --> 00:04:21,215
the teacher controls release.

103
00:04:21,905 --> 00:04:24,100
That gives time to review the marking and

104
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:26,800
prepare useful feedback before learners see it.

105
00:04:27,245 --> 00:04:29,180
The same assessment can then lead back

106
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:30,865
to the topic that needs attention.

107
00:04:31,665 --> 00:04:33,515
Let's follow that route as a student.

108
00:04:34,005 --> 00:04:36,840
The preparation library is organised by qualification,

109
00:04:37,465 --> 00:04:40,060
subject and topic. It includes AS

110
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:43,100
and A levels, IGCSE, IB, AP, SAT,

111
00:04:43,485 --> 00:04:44,980
IELTS and national preparation.

112
00:04:45,745 --> 00:04:49,440
Check the actual unit list, because
coverage differs between subjects.

113
00:04:50,125 --> 00:04:51,480
Inside a lesson, choose

114
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,840
the complete text or a guided view.

115
00:04:54,385 --> 00:04:57,480
Worked examples and recall practice have their own places.

116
00:04:58,185 --> 00:04:59,235
Read the explanation,

117
00:04:59,925 --> 00:05:02,200
try a question before revealing its answer,

118
00:05:02,625 --> 00:05:05,220
and compare the method rather than only the final number.

119
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:08,260
Some lessons have a separate visual explanation.

120
00:05:09,045 --> 00:05:10,940
Here, changing the denominator

121
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:13,380
changes the size of each fraction part.

122
00:05:13,865 --> 00:05:16,500
With three shaded parts, moving from quarters to

123
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:19,520
eighths changes three quarters into three eighths.

124
00:05:20,085 --> 00:05:22,235
You can see why the amount becomes smaller.

125
00:05:22,985 --> 00:05:25,285
Other available models include straight lines,

126
00:05:25,665 --> 00:05:26,465
right triangles,

127
00:05:26,945 --> 00:05:27,360
derivatives

128
00:05:27,545 --> 00:05:28,200
and area.

129
00:05:28,525 --> 00:05:31,400
In the triangle, changing theta changes the

130
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:35,200
opposite and adjacent sides while the hypotenuse stays fixed.

131
00:05:35,885 --> 00:05:37,840
The symbols describe that relationship.

132
00:05:38,565 --> 00:05:41,780
The full original lesson remains available when you switch back.

133
00:05:42,345 --> 00:05:44,680
Topic questions sit alongside the material.

134
00:05:45,325 --> 00:05:46,375
Write your reasoning,

135
00:05:46,565 --> 00:05:47,665
review the explanation

136
00:05:47,925 --> 00:05:49,475
and mark a question to revisit.

137
00:05:50,125 --> 00:05:53,760
Account features connect enrolled courses and saved progress,

138
00:05:54,105 --> 00:05:55,460
while flashcards let you

139
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:57,540
reveal an answer and rate your recall.

140
00:05:58,165 --> 00:06:00,100
There is also a dedicated IELTS centre.

141
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:04,040
Reading offers three full papers, each with three passages,

142
00:06:04,425 --> 00:06:06,220
forty questions and sixty minutes.

143
00:06:06,905 --> 00:06:10,060
The passage and questions sit together, with text highlighting,

144
00:06:10,405 --> 00:06:12,220
review flags and a navigator.

145
00:06:12,725 --> 00:06:15,720
After submitting, inspect the evidence behind the answers.

146
00:06:16,365 --> 00:06:18,065
The raw mark is practice feedback,

147
00:06:18,425 --> 00:06:19,475
not an official band.

148
00:06:19,945 --> 00:06:21,860
Listening has a full four-part paper

149
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:24,580
with forty questions and a continuous recording.

150
00:06:25,565 --> 00:06:29,200
Exam mode is once-only. Study mode adds replay controls,

151
00:06:29,645 --> 00:06:31,195
part shortcuts and transcripts.

152
00:06:31,965 --> 00:06:33,840
An interrupted exam attempt retains

153
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:36,520
responses for study and is clearly marked.

154
00:06:37,185 --> 00:06:42,060
The recording uses disclosed synthetic
voices and original FocusED material.

155
00:06:42,605 --> 00:06:44,560
Writing has three Academic papers,

156
00:06:44,885 --> 00:06:46,300
each with a visual Task One

157
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:47,580
and a Task Two essay.

158
00:06:48,425 --> 00:06:50,140
Choose timed or untimed practice,

159
00:06:50,665 --> 00:06:52,760
switch between tasks and watch the word counts.

160
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:56,520
Same-tab recovery keeps the original timed deadline.

161
00:06:57,165 --> 00:06:58,965
The self-check covers four criteria;

162
00:06:59,545 --> 00:07:03,680
optional AI feedback requires the
appropriate account access and credits.

163
00:07:04,325 --> 00:07:06,420
Speaking lessons are available, while

164
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,640
the dedicated Speaking mock is coming soon.

165
00:07:09,105 --> 00:07:11,400
SAT practice has original Reading and

166
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:14,200
Writing and Math modules, plus topic questions.

167
00:07:14,985 --> 00:07:17,240
In Math, open the College Board version

168
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:20,400
of Desmos inside the room. Enter the equations,

169
00:07:20,745 --> 00:07:23,160
inspect the graph and return to the answer.

170
00:07:23,785 --> 00:07:26,235
The clock continues while you use the calculator.

171
00:07:26,965 --> 00:07:27,765
Flag questions,

172
00:07:28,165 --> 00:07:29,180
eliminate choices

173
00:07:29,545 --> 00:07:31,600
and review explanations after submission.

174
00:07:32,325 --> 00:07:34,040
These are fixed practice modules.

175
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:36,540
They do not reproduce adaptive SAT

176
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:39,040
scoring or predict an official score.

177
00:07:39,505 --> 00:07:41,405
For Uzbekistan's national preparation,

178
00:07:41,925 --> 00:07:43,920
there are original Uzbek starter tracks for

179
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:47,340
Mathematics, Ona tili and CEFR or Multilevel.

180
00:07:47,905 --> 00:07:49,205
They include explanations,

181
00:07:49,545 --> 00:07:50,345
worked examples,

182
00:07:50,765 --> 00:07:51,615
answered practice

183
00:07:51,865 --> 00:07:53,015
and interactive checks.

184
00:07:53,525 --> 00:07:57,200
The national library keeps teaching
courses separate from textbook and

185
00:07:57,200 --> 00:08:00,880
official-guidance references,
with source and publication information.

186
00:08:01,665 --> 00:08:02,620
The starter tracks do

187
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:05,055
not claim to cover every certificate requirement.

188
00:08:05,465 --> 00:08:08,300
Around the study session, your account provides notes,

189
00:08:08,685 --> 00:08:10,260
flashcards and focus tools.

190
00:08:10,805 --> 00:08:13,040
Save and search a note. Turn a

191
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:15,800
difficult idea into a question you can test later.

192
00:08:16,345 --> 00:08:17,880
Use the study timer and breaks

193
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:19,940
to give one task a clear boundary.

194
00:08:20,545 --> 00:08:23,380
The weekly planner builds a template around your classes.

195
00:08:23,805 --> 00:08:26,100
The AI tutor can help explain a question,

196
00:08:26,445 --> 00:08:28,595
but you should still inspect its reasoning.

197
00:08:29,025 --> 00:08:30,175
Conversation retention,

198
00:08:30,785 --> 00:08:31,460
allowances

199
00:08:31,705 --> 00:08:34,140
and AI credits depend on the current plan.

200
00:08:34,685 --> 00:08:37,200
Check those details before starting paid AI

201
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:40,440
work. University planning has a separate workspace.

202
00:08:41,085 --> 00:08:43,160
Search the catalog, compare institutions

203
00:08:43,545 --> 00:08:44,780
and build a shortlist.

204
00:08:45,325 --> 00:08:48,200
Inspect the dates and source links behind a ranking,

205
00:08:48,525 --> 00:08:51,060
fee figure or historical admission rate.

206
00:08:51,525 --> 00:08:54,260
Then check the university's own current requirements.

207
00:08:54,877 --> 00:08:56,977
The application tools help keep deadlines,

208
00:08:57,517 --> 00:08:58,692
academic records,

209
00:08:59,157 --> 00:08:59,957
test attempts,

210
00:09:00,257 --> 00:09:01,057
essay drafts

211
00:09:01,237 --> 00:09:02,787
and private documents together.

212
00:09:03,397 --> 00:09:05,252
The roadmap organises the process.

213
00:09:05,797 --> 00:09:07,272
It cannot guarantee an offer

214
00:09:07,272 --> 00:09:09,852
or replace an institution's official instructions.

215
00:09:10,725 --> 00:09:13,140
Community spaces support study discussion.

216
00:09:13,785 --> 00:09:16,135
Direct messages remain with their participants,

217
00:09:16,545 --> 00:09:18,920
and private group creation needs approval.

218
00:09:19,625 --> 00:09:22,380
Parent access also requires the student's approval

219
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:25,940
before learning progress and released results can be shared.

220
00:09:26,525 --> 00:09:29,240
The course library can grow from inside the platform.

221
00:09:30,005 --> 00:09:32,480
An authorised editor can add a subtopic,

222
00:09:32,825 --> 00:09:33,625
write a lesson,

223
00:09:33,985 --> 00:09:35,580
attach a resource and create

224
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:37,500
a practice question with its answer.

225
00:09:38,205 --> 00:09:40,140
This matters when a teacher wants to add

226
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:43,320
an explanation for a mistake the class actually made.

227
00:09:43,845 --> 00:09:45,480
Administrators manage access,

228
00:09:45,845 --> 00:09:48,745
approvals and platform records through their own controls.

229
00:09:49,405 --> 00:09:52,405
These permissions are separate from ordinary student access.

230
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:55,225
Course editing is a publishing responsibility:

231
00:09:55,925 --> 00:09:57,025
check the explanation,

232
00:09:57,445 --> 00:10:00,420
answer and source before making material available.

233
00:10:01,025 --> 00:10:02,760
Finally, the interface has five

234
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:06,260
language options, appearance controls and responsive layouts.

235
00:10:06,925 --> 00:10:10,025
Those settings do not mean every lesson has five translations.

236
00:10:10,765 --> 00:10:14,600
Access options include the website,
supported home-screen installation,

237
00:10:15,265 --> 00:10:17,400
the Android package on the install page

238
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:20,520
and the Telegram entry point using the same account.

239
00:10:21,285 --> 00:10:23,240
An internet connection is still needed.

240
00:10:23,725 --> 00:10:26,220
You don't have to use every feature in one session.

241
00:10:26,545 --> 00:10:28,295
Start with the job in front of you:

242
00:10:28,385 --> 00:10:29,260
create a paper,

243
00:10:29,625 --> 00:10:32,900
review a response, prepare a class or learn one topic.

244
00:10:33,425 --> 00:10:34,660
Open FocusED,

245
00:10:35,025 --> 00:10:37,380
choose that job and work through the next step.
